For this demo, we'll use a simple REST API that returns a list of users. You can create a new API project using a tool like Postman or use an existing API.

**Step 3: Create a Refit client**

Create a new file called `refit_client.dart` and add the following code:
```dart
import 'package:http/http.dart' as http;
import 'package:refit/refit.dart';

part 'api_service.g.dart';

abstract class UserService {
  @GET('/users')
  Future<List<User>> getUsers();
}

@RestApi(baseUrl: 'https://your-api-url.com/api')
class Api {
  static final _client = http.Client();
  static final _userService = UserService(_client);
}
```
Here, we define a `UserService` interface that has a single method `getUsers()` that returns a list of `User` objects. We also define an `Api` class that provides a client instance using the `http` package.

**Step 4: Generate the API client code**

Generate the API client code using the following command:
```
flutter pub run refit_generator -o api_service.g.dart
```
This will generate a new file called `api_service.g.dart` that contains the implementation of the `UserService` interface.

**Step 5: Use the API client in your app**

Create a new file called `main.dart` and add the following code:
```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:refit_client/api_service.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(MyApp());
}

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      title: 'Refit Demo',
      home: MyHomePage(),
    );
  }
}

class MyHomePage extends StatefulWidget {
  @override
  _MyHomePageState createState() => _MyHomePageState();
}

class _MyHomePageState extends State<MyHomePage> {
  final _userService = Api._userService;

  Future<void> _getUsers() async {
    final users = await _userService.getUsers();
    print(users);
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(
        title: Text('Refit Demo'),
      ),
      body: Center(
        child: ElevatedButton(
          onPressed: _getUsers,
          child: Text('Get Users'),
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```
Here, we create a `MyHomePage` widget that has a button that calls the `_getUsers()` method when pressed. This method uses the `Api` client to call the `getUsers()` method and retrieve a list of users.

**Step 6: Run the app**

Run the app using the following command:
```
flutter run
```
This will start the app, and when you press the button, it will call the API and print the list of users to the console.

