PlaneU (short for "Plane Universal Coordinate") is a 3D coordinate system used in engineering and computer graphics. To convert two vectors into a PlaneU coordinate system, we need to calculate the normal vector of the plane, which is perpendicular to both input vectors.

Here's the code in C++:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <cmath>

// Structure to represent a 3D vector
struct Vector3 {
  double x, y, z;
};

// Calculate the cross product of two 3D vectors
Vector3 cross(const Vector3& v1, const Vector3& v2) {
  return Vector3(
    v1.y * v2.z - v1.z * v2.y,
    v1.z * v2.x - v1.x * v2.z,
    v1.x * v2.y - v1.y * v2.x
  );
